      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To summarize the research progress of the design and effectiveness of gender-specific prosthesis in total knee arthroplasty (TKA)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "The relevant literature on gender-specific prosthesis in recent years was extensively reviewed and analyzed."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Gender-specific prosthesis is designed according to the female knee joint anatomical characteristics. In theory, it should obtain better effectiveness. But a large number of clinical studies have shown that the knee function, pain, and satisfaction has no obvious advantage when compared with conventional prosthesis after TKA for female patient."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Comprehensive evaluation should be considered when gender-specific is selected; and the effectiveness needs further follow-up."
        }
      ]},
